From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwsim: refresh frame registrations after AP restart

OneWifi provisions a hwsim AP in stages.  The initial BSS setup registers
nl80211 management sockets plus the EAPOL packet socket.
Applying the EasyMesh-provided VAP configuration subsequently stops and starts
the AP through restart_interface().  Those registrations belong to the old BSS
lifecycle and must be released before start_bss() enters the normal HAL setup
path.

This produces a deceptive half-working VAP: beacons are transmitted and a
monitor interface on the same target wiphy receives a client's Open System
Authentication requests, while OneWifi's nl_recv_func never sees a readable
management socket and embedded hostapd sends no authentication response.
Restarting OneWifi recreates the registrations and immediately restores
authentication, proving that neither wmediumd delivery nor the steering target
is at fault.

Release the management and EAPOL receive paths before the STOP_AP/START_AP
transition.  start_bss() calls wifi_drv_set_operstate(), which creates exactly
one fresh set of registrations for the restarted BSS.  Refreshing them after
start_bss() is wrong: it destroys the new working socket, then collides with
its still-live kernel registrations and leaves an AP that beacons but cannot
answer authentication.  Limit the lifecycle correction to HWSIM_RADIO;
physical drivers retain registrations across their native AP restart.

Do not disturb the optional spurious-frame subscription.  It is not used for
authentication or EAPOL, its existing subscription remains usable across the
restart, and trying to replace it is rejected by mac80211_hwsim with EBUSY.
That diagnostic subscription must never turn an otherwise successful VAP
configuration into a failure.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
index 7e9f430..65f5e44 100644
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
@@ -6326,5 +6326,22 @@ int restart_interface(wifi_interface_info_t *interface)
         // exactly the case that needs it. Stopping an interface with no AP
         // running returns a harmless error which is logged and ignored.
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+        /* Registrations owned by the old hwsim BSS must be released before
+         * start_bss().  Its wifi_drv_set_operstate() callback creates the
+         * replacement registrations.  Replacing them after start_bss()
+         * destroys the newly working socket and collides with the live
+         * kernel registration, leaving a beaconing AP unable to authenticate
+         * clients. */
+        if (interface->mgmt_frames_registered) {
+            nl80211_unregister_mgmt_frames(interface);
+        }
+#ifndef EAPOL_OVER_NL
+        if (interface->data_frames_registered) {
+            unregister_data_frame_socket(interface);
+        }
+#endif /* EAPOL_OVER_NL */
+#endif /* HWSIM_RADIO */
+
         if (nl80211_enable_ap(interface, false) < 0) {
             wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d: interface:%s stop AP before restart returned an "
                 "error (expected when no AP was running)\n", __func__, __LINE__, interface_name);
-- 
